  "id": "COMPOUND:37753 - PROTEIN:4740",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential mechanism by which 4-Ketopinoresinol may interact with Serine/threonine-protein kinase pim-3, through a series of target-mediated pathways. The drug is implicated in targeting the T-cell surface glycoprotein CD3 zeta chain, which is a critical component of the T-cell receptor complex. This target is then engaged by (+)-Parviflorol and another compound, (1S,3R,8R,11S,12S,14R,15S,16R)-15-[(1S)-1-(dimethylamino)ethyl]-14-hydroxy-7,7,12,16-tetramethylpentacyclo[9.7.0.01,3.03,8.012,16]octadecan-6-one, both of which are known to inhibit Serine/threonine-protein kinase pim-3. The presence of multiple compounds that share the same target suggests a possible mechanism of action involving the inhibition of pim-3, potentially through a common pathway or distinct but related mechanisms. The evidence is supported by high scores in the scoring system, indicating a strong likelihood of a functional relationship. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for 4-Ketopinoresinol to modulate pim-3 activity, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the exact mechanism of action.",
